nodecode-apinex is a rewrite of Apinex-AI's Apinex-AI/hermes-provider-apinex:

https://github.com/Apinex-AI/hermes-provider-apinex
commit d838363f40c8c2ac3d0254c69c43cef11f9dec79

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 APInex (LICENSE)

The rewrite keeps what the plugin gives a Hermes user: the two provider ids,
`apinex` for the Claude family over APInex's Messages endpoint and
`apinex-openai` for the GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek, GLM, Qwen, Kimi, Grok, MiniMax,
MiMo, Muse and Hunyuan models and the Free tier over the OpenAI-compatible
endpoint, both at https://api.apinex.bond/v1 and both on the one
APINEX_API_KEY; the per-model capability matrix (its context windows and
vision flags); the rule that splits the gateway's model list between the two
wires, dropping media, embedding, speech and non-tool entries; and the
never-answer-another-provider's-key behaviour it shared with its runtime.
What was left out is above the plugin's own work and not in it: the row is a
Nodecode catalog row rather than a Hermes ProviderProfile, its two hooks are
Nodecode's, and the model list it fetched from /v1/models at run time is
bundled in models.json, laid out as that endpoint lists it, so nothing here
dials the gateway. The gateway addresses and the model rows are the
original's data. Nothing of the original's Python is included.
